# .trivyignore — selva-office
#
# Each entry MUST cite (1) why the upstream fix is unavailable or unworkable
# and (2) the specific reason this codebase is not exposed to the
# vulnerability's preconditions. Re-evaluate every entry on every CI failure.

# CVE-2024-23342 — python-ecdsa "Minerva" timing side-channel attack on
# ECDSA signature operations. Upstream has no fix (see
# https://github.com/tlsfuzzer/python-ecdsa/security/advisories/GHSA-wj6h-64fc-37mp).
# selva-office is NOT exposed:
#   - ecdsa is transitive-only, pulled in by python-jose 3.5.0 via
#     algorithm-dispatch tables; we never `import ecdsa` directly.
#   - The ONLY jwt.decode() call site (apps/nexus-api/nexus_api/auth.py:91)
#     pins algorithms=["RS256"] (RSA), so python-jose never hands a token
#     to ecdsa for verification, even when an attacker supplies the JWT.
#   - No other call site uses python-jose.
# The Minerva attack additionally requires precise per-operation timing
# measurements against the running process, which our internal-API
# traffic shape does not afford to a remote attacker. Re-evaluate if
# (a) any new code path adds an ECDSA-keyed JWT alg to the whitelist,
# (b) python-jose is ever invoked on attacker-controlled tokens with a
# permissive algorithms= list, or (c) python-ecdsa ships a fix.
CVE-2024-23342
